Volatile Service Runbook

Summary
The volatile-etl-service is an AWS Lambda solution. It takes a trade text file as an input, extracts the data, performs simple
transformations on the data, and produces our output file. The transformation involves filtering the trades by product type, 
mapping from Vanguard schema to the regulator’s schema and enriching the trades with a counterparty LEI from a static file.
It runs on a cron schedule of every 5 minutes. The processing is deterministic.

Inputs
src/resources/input/CounterPartyStatic.txt
src/resources/input/trades.txt

Outputs
src/resources/output/report.csv

Application Triggers
Cron schedule, every 5 minutes. * /5 * * * *

Troubleshooting
Missing Trade File
Common issues include:
- AWS outage, check if there is an incident email from AWS_incidents@volatilecorp.com
- Upstream availability issue, check if there is an incident email from trades_oms@volatilecorp.com 

Missing Report File
Business users expect the report file by 10am and if they do not receive by then, they reach out to the development team via email. The development team need 
to investigate the cause of the missing report file. Common issues include:
- AWS outage, check if there is an incident email from AWS_incidents@volatilecorp.com
- Trades file is missing headers. To resolve manually add the headers

Wrong Counterparty LEI
Counterparty LEI is obtained from the CounterPartyStatic.txt static file and used to enrich trade information using OMS counterparty code from the trades.txt file in the transformation 
to the report csv file. Sometimes new LEIs are created and the CounterPartyStatic.txt static file becomes stale, resulting in a default LEI being populated. The 
application creates informational logs when this occurs, and the development team is alerted of the logs. Business users of the application may also reach out via 
email to let us know that LEI enrichment was incorrect. To resolve this issue reach out to the business via email at data_team@volatilecorp.com to obtain the 
missing LEI mapping and update the CounterPartyStatic.txt file.

Elevation Process
1. The application is deployed to the us-east-1 primary region and the eu-west-2 secondary region.
2. Avoid elevation between 9am -2pm when availability is critical for the business

Developer Requirements
The application uses Python 3.9 deployed on AWS Lambda
